📌 Shortcut Trick yaad rakhne ka:
Authentication = Identity check ("Tum kaun ho?")
Authorization = Permission check ("Tum kya kar sakte ho?")

Cookies:- 
Browser ke andar chhoti si file hoti hai jisme server tumhare baare me chhoti info store karta hai (jaise login token, user id, etc.).
Jab tum same website pe wapas aate ho, browser wo cookie server ko bhej deta hai, taaki server tumhe pehchan sake.

Authentication me help :-
Cookie me ek session ID ya token store hota hai.
Jab tum next request bhejte ho, server cookie dekh ke confirm karta hai ki tum already logged in ho.

Authorization me help :- 
Cookie me tumhare role (admin, user, guest) ka info ho sakta hai.
Server is role ke hisaab se decide karta hai ki tumhe kaunsa page ya action allowed hai.


JWT -> JSON Web Token
JWT (JSON Web Token) → A digital token used to verify a user's identity without storing session on the server.
       JWT ka fayda:
       Server ko session store karne ki zaroorat nahi hoti (stateless).
       Secure tarike se info transfer hoti hai.

Bcrypt ->
bcrypt → A library to securely hash and compare passwords so they’re not stored in plain text.
     Fayda:
     Agar database hack ho jaye, hacker ko asli password nahi milega.
     Salt hone ki wajah se same password ka hash bhi alag hota hai.

     Example with salt:
Agar 10 users ka password 1234 hai, to sabka hash same hoga → easy to guess.
Password: 1234 + Random Salt ($%&8#)
Final Hash: 8hd7ajd8ajsd...

Dusre user ka password 1234 + Alag Salt (@1ab!)
Final Hash: 9f72ns7y28ds...
👉 Ab dono ka hash different hoga, even though password same tha.


